cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these colourings, tables, certificates or programs, please cite them as below, together with the earlier work credited in README.md."
type: dataset
title: "Computational results on Erdős problems"
abstract: "Erdős #160: h(77) = 7, so h(N) is known for every N <= 77. Erdős #311: delta(N) exactly for every N <= 60. Erdős #461: the minimum over n of f(n,t) exactly for every t <= 54 and even t <= 64. Erdős #535: f_3(N) exactly for every N <= 64. Erdős #624: H(n) for n = 2..11 (f arbitrary). Erdős #902: no Cayley tournament on fewer than 67 vertices has property S_4. Erdős #982: a Lean 4 proof of the cases n <= 13 (settled earlier by others), with checks of its certificates. Erdős #1159: the least cap of a blocking set in twelve projective planes of order at most 16. Erdős #1210: M(n) exactly for every 3 <= n <= 1794. Computed values and finite cases only; none settles its problem."
authors:
  - family-names: Canli
    given-names: Arhan
    affiliation: Quantavane
    email: arhan@quantavane.com
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://quantavane.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arhancanli/quantavane-erdos-results"
keywords:
  - Erdős problems
  - arithmetic progressions
  - unit fractions
  - tournaments
  - Cayley digraphs
  - Lean 4
  - projective planes
  - SAT certificates
